 "parsed": {
  "count": 1,
  "rationale": "With no defences the attacker can win: phish (foothold_workstation, stolen_user), then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So 0 is not enough. Deploying mfa:admin alone stops it. It blocks auth_dc and auth_adfs, the only ways to get foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. Without those footholds, admin_dc and admin_adfs cannot be reached. Without admin_dc or admin_adfs, stolen_dbadmin cannot be obtained, since only dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs produce it. Every auth technique for db, fileserver and backup requires stolen_dbadmin, so no admin on those hosts is possible and no exfiltrate technique can fire. The minimum is therefore 1 control: mfa:admin."
 },
